      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-02-25_WidnesExaminer_art0119" n="art0119">
        <head>LETTERS TO THE EDITOR. LABOUR DEMONSTRATION. MR A. H. CROSFIELD REPLIES TO HIS CRITICS.</head>
        <p>LETTERS TO THE EDITOR. LABOUR DEMONSTRATION. MR A. H. CROSFIELD REPLIES TO HIS CRITICS.</p>
        <p>NOTICE TO CORRESPONDENT. Authors of letters intended for publication must in all cases sent their names and addresses to the Editor as a guarantee of good faith. Matters intended for publication must be written on bide only of the paper and sent in, if possible, not ater than Thursday.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-02-25_WidnesExaminer_art0120" n="art0120">
        <head>Sugar Convention.</head>
        <p>The Sugar Convention.</p>
        <p>The Socialist Vote.</p>
        <p>MR. JOSEPH HOWES ON THE IRISH QUESTION.</p>
