      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-02-25_WidnesExaminer_art0123" n="art0123">
        <head>A. nATHBONE.</head>
        <p>A. nATHBONE.</p>
        <p>Warrington Froghall Cycling Club. The first annual dance in connection with the above club was held in die Fairfield Schools on Thursday evening, and notwithstanding the fact that there were four other dances being held the same night, it turned out a complete success, about 00 participating in the evening's enjoyment. Mr. Edward Draper, the popular president of the club kindly consented to officiate as N.C. and was ably seconded in his efforts by Messrs. F. G. Bate, W. and E. Pickles and H. Rogns, as stewarts. Delightful music was rendered by Mr. Tom Taylors's band dancing being indulged in till 2 a.m. The catering was left in the capable hands of Mrs. Atkinson, this being sufficient to ensure complete satisfaction in that department. The proceedings came to a close all too soon, and it was with feelings almost of regret that the various friends parted. This dance augurs well for the future, as the club is only in its infancy, this being the first year of its inaugura- tion.• Mention might also be made here of a very successful dinner which wss held in the Lion Hotel on January sth last, also presided over by Mr. Draper. This was confined to members only, and paid for out of club funds. Cycling clubs, as a rule, in their first year, seldom have a very large banking account. The working of the past year reflects gr..!at credit upon the officials and all connected.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-02-25_WidnesExaminer_art0124" n="art0124">
        <gap reason="ocrQuality" quantity="0" unit="words">
