        <p>('IOUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON- N.) THB WATHR COMMITTIIII of the Council of the Borough invite THROB:IS for the supply for six months of best VIRING SLACK In qusntities es follows : (a) About 20 tons, more or less, per week at their Winwick Pumping station. (0) About 16 tons, more or less, per week et their Houghton Green Pumping Station. I Also the supply of house coal to be delivered at Winwick and Houghton Green Pumpin,g Stations, Appleton Reservoir and Bank House, in such quantities as may be required. Tenderers must name the pit and seam from which the slack and coal will be taken. the contractor 'shall pay all persons engaged or employed by them on the works the rates of wages recognized in the district and shall observe such hours of labour as are gener- ally accepted as fair in each trade and shall from time to time whenever required so to do by the Council produce to them such evidence as they may deem sufficient that they are paying such wages and observing such hourel. Tenders to be addressed "The Chdirman,Water Committee Town Hall, Warrington " to be securely fastened, endorsed t' Tenster for Slack," and delivered not later than 10 a.m., 11th Welch. 19,5. The lowest or any tender not necessarily accepted. JAMBS DRAS. A M.1.C.H., Water Engineer. Municipal Offices. Warrington. 23rd Yea., 1905.</p>
        <p>WARRINEITON lON.-TENDERS.- PERSONS willing to CONTR&amp;OT for the supply of any of thi, undermentioned articles from Lady Day to Michaelmas next, to be delivered free of expense at the Workhouse or at the Cottage Homes. at such times and in such quantities as the Board of Guardians shall direct, are requested to send in tenders addressed to me before four o'clock a.m. on Tuesday the 7th day of March. 1505. TENDERS ARE RhQUIkED FOR:— Coal and Slack Groceries and Necessaries Clogs Beef and Mutton Shoes and Slippers Joints for Officers Coffins Flom- and Oatmeal Brushes Bread for Cottage Homes Leather Drapery &amp;c. Tailors Goods. Separate Tenders must be sent for the Workhouse and Cottage Homes, and samples of the articles required may be seen at each institution. The Tenders for fuel must specify the pit and seam from which it will be supplied. Forms of Tender and instructions to persons tendering, (which must be strictly compiled with) may be obtained from the Master of the Workhouse alai the Superintendent of the Cottage Homes respectively. Each contractor must be prepared to enter (if required) into security for the due performance of his contract. Tho Guardians do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any tender: All contract accannts will be paid quarterly. Special attention is called to the (act that the methods of dealing wit. , and of obtaining tenders, have beers revised. New samples provided and these should be inspected by intending 1 contractors before filli Lig up tender forms. By Order J. 0. SUTTON. Clerk to the Guardian., Bewsey Chambers. Warrington. February 23rd, 1905.</p>
